prompts.text:
I have been meaning to do a prompt for viruses and all these other topics. Here is an attempt: 

2x2 grid, 16:9, AI picks subjects different from examples: :root {
    --subject: "$adaptive immune recognition"; /* e.g. T cell - dendritic cell synapse, Antibody affinity maturation, CAR-T engagement, MHC presentation */
    --representation: "Binding kinetics to cellular warfare";
}

# canvas {
    background: # 100a14;
}

# subject_render {
    mask-image: none;
    render-left-side: "Pure immunology: affinity and avidity equations, MHC-peptide binding prediction, Hill equation for receptor occupancy, clonal selection theory, cytokine kinetic curves, somatic hypermutation rate — all in clean white annotation on dark tissue-paper texture.";
    render-center: "The synapse forming: receptor clustering at the immunological synapse, signalling cascade with phosphorylation events, cytoskeletal rearrangement, germinal centre reaction with B cells competing for antigen, antibody affinity increasing over generations.";
    render-right-side: "Photoreal physical immunity: a T cell and dendritic cell in contact with real membrane texture and microvilli, an antibody Y-shape with glycan chains and disulfide bonds, a vaccine vial with aluminium adjuvant and a syringe, a histology slide with stained lymph node germinal centres.";
    transition-zone: "The Kd value becoming the actual tightness of the molecular embrace. The clonal selection arrow turning into real cell division.";
}
